```java
interface ReportGenerator { void generate(List<Order> orders); }

// Abstract creator + template method
abstract class ReportService {
    protected abstract ReportGenerator createGenerator(); // factory method

    public void export(List<Order> orders) {              // template method
        var generator = createGenerator();                // delegated to subclass
        System.out.println("Fetching orders...");
        generator.generate(orders);                       // works via interface
        System.out.println("Done");
    }
}

class PdfReportService extends ReportService {
    protected ReportGenerator createGenerator() { return new PdfReportGenerator(); }
}
class ExcelReportService extends ReportService {
    protected ReportGenerator createGenerator() { return new ExcelReportGenerator(); }
}

// Usage
ReportService service = new PdfReportService(); // choose creator at runtime
service.export(List.of(new Order(1, "Laptop")));
// Add CsvReportService -> new class only; ReportService never changes.
```

*Simple Factory edits a switch to add a type; Factory Method adds a subclass — that's the OCP difference.*

