```java
interface Notifier { void send(String msg); }
interface NotifierFactory { Notifier create(String type); }

class OrderService {
    private final NotifierFactory factory;          // injected seam
    OrderService(NotifierFactory factory) { this.factory = factory; }
    void placeOrder(Order order, String type) {
        factory.create(type).send("Order " + order.getId());
    }
}

// Production wiring
class RealNotifierFactory implements NotifierFactory {
    public Notifier create(String t) { return t.equals("sms") ? new SmsNotifier() : new EmailNotifier(); }
}

// Test: inject a factory that returns a fake -> no real I/O
NotifierFactory testFactory = type -> msg -> {}; // returns a no-op Notifier
var service = new OrderService(testFactory);
service.placeOrder(new Order(123, "Laptop"), "email"); // fast, isolated, no email sent
```

*The seam is the injected factory; tests control what it returns.*

